{"id":"G4982","lemma":"σῴζω","transliteration":"sōzō","sayIt":"sōzō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to save","meaning":"σώζω (on the more accurate σῴζω, see WH, Intr., §410; Bl., §3, 1-3),\n[in LXX chiefly for ישׁע hi., also for מלט ni., נצל ni., etc. ;]\nto save from peril, injury or suffering: Mat.8:25, Mrk.13:20, Luk.23:35, al.; τ. ψυχήν, Mat.16:25, al.; before ἐκ, Jhn.12:27, Heb.5:7, Ju 5; of healing, restoring to health: Mat.9:22, Mrk.5:34, al. In NT, esp. of salvation from spiritual disease and death, in which sense it is \"spoken of in Scripture as either (1) past, (2) present, or (3) future, according as redemption, grace, or glory is the point in view. Thus (1) Rom.8:24, Eph.2:5, 8 2Ti.1:9, Tit.3:5; (2) Act.2:47, 1Co.1:18, 15:2, 2Co.2:15; (3) Mat.10:22, Rom.13:11, Php.2:12, Heb.9:28\" (Vau. on Rom.5:9). Seq. ἀπό, Mat.1:21, Act.2:40, Rom.5:9; ἐκ, Jas.5:20, Ju 23 (cf. Cremer, 532ff.).\n(AS)","glosses":["saved","save","healed","has healed","may be saved","being saved"],"count":98,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"will save","kjv":"shall save"}},{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"save us","kjv":"save"}},{"chapterId":"mat-9","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"I will be healed"}},{"chapterId":"mat-9","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"has healed","kjv":"hath made"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be saved"}},{"chapterId":"mat-14","v":30,"renderings":{"bsb":"save","kjv":"save"}},{"chapterId":"mat-16","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"to save","kjv":"save"}},{"chapterId":"mat-19","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"be saved"}},{"chapterId":"mat-24","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be saved"}},{"chapterId":"mat-24","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"would be saved","kjv":"be saved"}},{"chapterId":"mat-27","v":40,"renderings":{"bsb":"save","kjv":"save"}},{"chapterId":"mat-27","v":42,"renderings":{"bsb":"He saved","kjv":"He saved"}},{"chapterId":"mat-27","v":49,"renderings":{"bsb":"to save","kjv":"to save"}},{"chapte